## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The primary searcher is a prospective renter, most often a young professional, recent graduate, or relocator, who is in the early-to-mid discovery stage of searching for a one-bedroom apartment in New York City. They do not yet have a clear sense of what they can expect to pay, which boroughs or neighborhoods fit their budget, or how the NYC rental process differs from other cities. Their specific problem is a gap between what they know (they need a one-bedroom in NYC) and what they need to know (what it will cost, where to look, and how the process works). Based on the SERP analysis, they expect a practical reference guide with cost data by area, clear affordability benchmarks, and enough process guidance to take a concrete next step.

