**Writing instruction:** This section covers a decision framework that Claude surfaced in its AI response (Data Source 3) but that does not appear in competitor content. It reframes the cost comparison between Manhattan and outer boroughs as a commute-cost equation, not just a rent comparison. The writing agent must present this as a practical calculation: a $1,600/month rent differential between a Hell's Kitchen apartment and a Jackson Heights apartment may narrow significantly when subway commute time, monthly MetroCard cost, and time-as-cost are factored in. Do not present this as a formula. Present it as a decision question the renter should ask themselves. Include one concrete example comparing two specific apartments in two specific neighborhoods with commute time and monthly cost delta. This section constitutes information gain over competitors.

